{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And he shall lean and slaughter.</b> The owners — to serve in it before their Creator up to receiving [the blood] and onward, which is the commandment upon the priesthood. <b>And he shall lean and slaughter:</b> just as leaning is done by those who are pure, so slaughter is done by those who are pure. <b>And he shall lean and slaughter:</b> in the place where they lean, they slaughter. <b>And he shall lean and slaughter:</b> immediately after leaning comes slaughter." "<b>A young bull.</b> An expression of youthfulness, to exclude one that is excessively old and one that is diseased, based on ״הקריבהו נא לפחתך״." "<b>A young bull before YHWH.</b> And the slaughterer is not before YHWH. Shimon HaTimni says: from where do we know that the hand of the slaughterer must be on the inner side of the animal being slaughtered? Scripture says: ״את בן הבקר לפני ה׳״." "<b>The sons of Aaron.</b> That they should not be elders who tremble, as our Sages said: from when is a priest disqualified? From when he trembles." "<b>Aaron.</b> Like Aaron, who has no blemish. <b>The priests</b> — and not profaned priests; those with blemishes and profaned priests are excluded."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:09:35.707187864Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}